:[{"id":"WJ10285","code":"100"}]}},"clans":[{"id":"GI111815","name":{"zh":"襄阳蒯氏","en":"The Kuai clan of Xiangyang"},"years":["0","999"],"desc":{"zh":"出自姬姓，春秋时晋大夫蒯得之后。西汉初名臣蒯通为其先祖，家族于东汉时徙居襄阳中庐，成为当地大姓。蒯良、蒯越是刘表“单马入宜城”后平定荆州的核心智囊。曹操得荆州后称“不喜得荆州，喜得蒯异度耳”，蒯越官至九卿光禄勋。家族通过联姻与西晋皇室建立关系，在魏晋时期持续保有政治影响力。","en":"Descended from the Ji surname, the lineage of Kuai De, grand master of Jin during the Spring and Autumn period. The early Western Han statesman Kuai Tong was their ancestor. The Family relocated to Zhonglu in Xiangyang during the Eastern Han and became a prominent local clan. Kuai Liang and Kuai Yue were Liu Biao's core strategists after he entered Yicheng on a single Horse to pacify Jing Province. After taking Jing Province, Cao Cao remarked, ‘I rejoice not in gaining Jing Province, but in gaining Kuai Yidu.’ Kuai Yue rose to the rank of Minister of the Household. Through marriage alliances, the Family established ties with the Western Jin imperial house, maintaining political influence throughout the Wei and Jin dynasties."},"talent":{"military":"3","commerce":"4","politics":"6"}}],"friendGroups":[{"story":"S10802","members":["WJ10058","WJ10285","WJ10151","WJ10522","WJ10150","WJ10382","WJ10152","WJ10286"]},{"story":"S10802","members":["WJ10058","WJ10285","WJ10830","WJ10914"]},{"story":"S10615","members":["WJ10058","WJ10285","WJ10151","WJ10522","WJ10150","WJ10382","WJ10152","WJ10286"]},{"story":"S10615","members":["WJ10058","WJ10285","WJ10830","WJ10914"]},{"story":"S10402","members":["WJ10058","WJ10285","WJ10151","WJ10522","WJ10150","WJ10382","WJ10152","WJ10286"]},{"story":"S10402","members":["WJ10058","WJ10285","WJ10830","WJ10914"]},{"story":"S10415","members":["WJ10058","WJ10285","WJ10151","WJ10522","WJ10150","WJ10382","WJ10152","WJ10286"]},{"story":"S10415","members":["WJ10058","WJ10285","WJ10830","WJ10914"]},{"story":"S10202","members":["WJ10058","WJ10285","WJ10151","WJ10522","WJ10150","WJ10382","WJ10152","WJ10286"]},{"story":"S10202","members":["WJ10058","WJ10285","WJ108